From fee8a8dab4f5e23b13bb9dbcf0ab657e4abaa578 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:24:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lapin UX: windows reopen at their last size and place

Wayland apps can't place their own windows, and cosmic-comp only keeps a
window's geometry while it exists. In the Lapin session the floating
layout now notes each app's window size and position (per app id, with
the output) and saves them to $XDG_STATE_HOME/lapin-ux/window-geometry
when a window closes; a new window of that app opens there when nothing
else decides its place (no position asked for, not a dialog, not a
window coming back from minimize). Kept on screen; centred on another
output. Maximized and snapped windows aren't noted.

Refs #42
